The couples dance each week in a live show. The judges score each performance out of ten. The couples are then ranked according to the judges' scores and given points according to their rank, with the lowest scored couple receiving one point, and the highest scored couple receiving the most points (the maximum number of points available depends on the number of couples remaining in the competition). The public are also invited to vote for their favourite couples, and the couples are ranked again according to the number of votes they receive, again receiving points; the couple with the fewest votes receiving one point, and the couple with the most votes receiving the most points.

The points for judges' score and public vote are then added together, and the two couples with the fewest points are placed in the bottom two. If two couples have equal points, the points from the public vote are given precedence. As with the previous series, the bottom two couples have to perform a dance-off on the results show. Based on that performance alone, each judge then votes on which couple should stay and which couple should leave, with [[Len Goodman]], as head judge, having the last and [[Casting vote|deciding vote]].

==Professional dancers==
On 28 June 2016, the list of professionals who were returning for the fourteenth series was revealed. Professionals from the last series who did not return included [[Ola Jordan]], [[Tristan MacManus]], [[Kristina Rihanoff]], [[Gleb Savchenko]], and [[Aliona Vilani]]. They were replaced by [[Katya Jones]] and her husband [[Neil Jones (dancer)|Neil Jones]], ''[[Burn the Floor]]'' dancer [[Gorka Márquez]], former ''[[Dancing with the Stars (American TV series)|Dancing with the Stars]]'' troupe member [[Oksana Platero]], and ex-[[Britain's Got Talent (series 7)|Britain's Got Talent contestants]] [[AJ Pritchard]] and [[Chloe Hewitt]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/mediacentre/latestnews/2016/bbc-one-new-dancers-strictly|title=Three new professional dancers join the Strictly Come Dancing line-up for 2016|publisher=BBC Media Centre|date=26 July 2016|access-date=26 July 2016}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/webarchive/https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bbc.co.uk%2Fblogs%2Fstrictlycomedancing%2Fentries%2Ff245a196-3e06-4dd4-bdc7-a9de97ff0226|title=BBC Blogs – Strictly Come Dancing – 2016 Strictly Professional Dancer line up revealed!|date=28 June 2016|publisher=BBC|access-date=14 July 2016}}</ref> Chloe Hewitt and Neil Jones were not partnered with a celebrity, although they were on standby for any pro who might have been injured or unable to compete, and also performed in group dances and appeared on the ''Strictly'' companion programme, ''[[Strictly Come Dancing: It Takes Two|It Takes Two]]''.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.tellymix.co.uk/reality-tv/strictly-come-dancing/275407-strictly-come-dancing-2016-two-pros-dont-get-celebrity-partners.html|title=Two of Strictly's new pros don't get celebrity partners|last=Darvill|first=Josh|date=1 September 2016|publisher=Tellymix|access-date=1 September 2016}}</ref>

==Couples==
This series featured fifteen celebrity contestants. On 8 August 2016, former [[Shadow Chancellor]] [[Ed Balls]] was announced as the first celebrity contestant,<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/webarchive/https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bbc.co.uk%2Fblogs%2Fstrictlycomedancing%2Fentries%2F5226be8c-cd7b-4ca9-8fe8-0bfcbc4e3b2e|title=Ed Balls revealed as the first Strictly celeb of 2016!|publisher=BBC |date=8 August 2016 |access-date=8 August 2016}}</ref> with more celebrities being announced throughout the month. The line up was completed on 22 August on ''[[The One Show]]''.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/strictly-come-dancing/news/a804713/strictly-come-dancing-2016-lesley-joseph-confirmed-contestant |title=Lesley Joseph confirmed as a contestant for this year |website=Digital Spy |date=22 August 2016 |access-date=25 August 2016}}</ref>

On 11 October, [[Will Young]] announced that he was leaving the show for "personal reasons".<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/entertainment-arts-37622797|title=Will Young quits Strictly Come Dancing|date=11 October 2016|work=BBC News |access-date=11 October 2016}}</ref>
